---
import ResearchReport from "@/components/temporal-research-agent/ResearchReport.md";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const root = "/temporal-research-agent";
---

<PageLayout
  title="Durable literature-review agents"
  kicker="The live research product"
  intro="A cited report produced by the Temporal-backed research pipeline, with its method and provenance kept close at hand."
  description="The completed research output from a durable literature-review Workflow using live SciX and Code Intelligence Digest evidence."
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="research-output">
    <nav class="research-output__nav" aria-label="Research output links">
      <a href={root}>← Case study</a>
      <a href={`${root}/readme`}>README</a>
      <a href={`${root}/research-output/report.md`}>Raw Markdown</a>
      <a href={`${root}/research-output/manifest.json`}>Provenance manifest</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="research-output__summary" aria-labelledby="run-summary">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Completed run</p>
        <h2 id="run-summary">Retrieval survived long enough to become synthesis</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        We ran the same four-angle Workflow against the live SciX and Code
        Intelligence Digest indexes. It finished with <strong>4 completed
        angles</strong>, <strong>0 failed angles</strong>, and <strong>48
        retrieved records</strong>: 24 from SciX and 24 from Code Intelligence
        Digest.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="research-output__method" aria-labelledby="pipeline-heading">
      <header>
        <p class="kicker">How the report was made</p>
        <h2 id="pipeline-heading">The durable research pipeline</h2>
      </header>
      <ol aria-label="Durable research pipeline">
        <li>
          <code>research_angle</code>
          <span>
            searches both providers and stores the full responses as durable
            evidence artifacts.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>verify_evidence</code>
          <span>
            re-reads the artifacts and checks their content hashes before
            evidence enters the report.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>synthesize_section</code>
          <span>
            turns each question’s normalized evidence into findings with
            readable, linked citations.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>finalize_review</code>
          <span>
            calls SciX <code>synthesize_findings</code> across the combined
            scholarly working set, then writes the report and provenance
            manifest.
          </span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <aside class="research-output__finding" aria-labelledby="synthesized-finding">
      <p class="kicker">Synthesized finding</p>
      <h2 id="synthesized-finding">
        Durability is a property of the whole research pipeline
      </h2>
      <p>
        Temporal preserves orchestration decisions and retries nondeterministic
        work, but correct recovery still depends on idempotent tool contracts,
        durable artifacts with provenance, and tests that verify intermediate
        state and output fidelity.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <section class="research-output__lane" aria-labelledby="digest-contribution">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Engineering evidence</p>
        <h2 id="digest-contribution">What Code Intelligence Digest contributed</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          The 24 Digest records include practitioner material and indexed
          technical discussions. In the report, the provider appears as a
          readable label and every title links directly to its source; internal
          item IDs remain in the provenance manifest.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.morling.dev/blog/building-durable-execution-engine-with-sqlite/">
              Building a Durable Execution Engine with SQLite
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/LLMDevs/comments/1r0fzyc/replay_is_not_reexecution_the_reproducibility_gap/">
              Replay is not re-execution
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://devops.com/agentic-ai-in-observability-platforms-empowering-autonomous-sre/">
              Agentic AI in Observability Platforms
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="research-output__report prose" aria-label="Completed live research report">
      <ResearchReport />
    </article>

    <footer class="research-output__footer">
      <p>
        The readable report omits repository-specific source IDs. The
        <a href={`${root}/research-output/manifest.json`}>provenance manifest</a>
        preserves them with content hashes, retrieval timestamps, artifact
        references, and provider lanes.
      </p>
      <a href={`${root}/research-output/synthesis.json`}>Inspect the SciX synthesis output →</a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .research-output {
    padding-block-end: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .research-output > * + * {
    margin-block-start: clamp(var(--space-xl), 8vw, var(--space-3xl));
  }

  .research-output__nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    border-block: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .research-output__nav a {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 3.5rem;
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-s);
    align-items: center;
    border-inline-end: var(--border-hairline);
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .research-output__nav a:hover {
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .research-output__summary,
  .research-output__lane {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(15rem, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .research-output__summary h2,
  .research-output__lane h2,
  .research-output__method h2,
  .research-output__finding h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .research-output__summary .kicker,
  .research-output__lane .kicker,
  .research-output__method .kicker,
  .research-output__finding .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs);
  }

  .research-output__summary > p,
  .research-output__lane p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .research-output__method {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(15rem, 4fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .research-output__method ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    counter-reset: pipeline;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .research-output__method li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-s);
    padding-block: var(--space-m);
    border-top: var(--border-hairline);
    counter-increment: pipeline;
  }

  .research-output__method li::before {
    content: counter(pipeline, decimal-leading-zero);
    grid-row: span 2;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .research-output__method code {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .research-output__method span {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .research-output__finding {
    max-width: 52rem;
    padding: clamp(var(--space-l), 5vw, var(--space-2xl));
    border-inline-start: 0.35rem solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
  }

  .research-output__finding h2 {
    max-width: 19ch;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }

  .research-output__finding > p:last-child {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: var(--space-m) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .research-output__lane ul {
    margin: var(--space-m) 0 0;
    padding-inline-start: 1.2rem;
  }

  .research-output__lane li + li {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .research-output__report {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 78ch;
    padding-block: var(--space-xl);
    border-block: var(--border-hairline);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  :global(.research-output__report > h1:first-child) {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  :global(.research-output__report h2) {
    margin-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  :global(.research-output__report h3) {
    margin-block: var(--space-l) var(--space-xs);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  :global(.research-output__report h4) {
    margin-block: var(--space-m) var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }

  :global(.research-output__report li + li) {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
  }

  :global(.research-output__report a) {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .research-output__footer {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(14rem, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-l);
    border-top: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .research-output__footer p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .research-output__footer > a {
    justify-self: end;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .research-output__summary,
    .research-output__method,
    .research-output__lane,
    .research-output__footer {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-l);
    }

    .research-output__nav a {
      width: 50%;
      border-bottom: var(--border-hairline);
    }

    .research-output__finding {
      padding: var(--space-l);
    }

    .research-output__footer > a {
      justify-self: start;
    }
  }
</style>
